outram-park-mpi
Part of Outram Park (outram-park-backend).

This crate is an independent, pure-Rust translation of a SUBSET of MPICH
  https://www.mpich.org   (code: https://github.com/pmodels/mpich)
MPICH is a high-performance, widely-portable implementation of the MPI (Message
Passing Interface) standard, developed at Argonne National Laboratory (ANL) and
by the MPICH collaboration. "MPI" names the standard (from the MPI Forum) whose
API surface this crate implements; "MPICH" names the reference implementation
whose semantics and (in later milestones) collective algorithms are translated.

WHAT IS TRANSLATED. This crate re-implements MPI-3 concepts in idiomatic Rust:
communicator/rank/size, predefined datatypes, point-to-point messaging, and
(planned) collective operations. The current milestone provides a shared-memory,
threads-as-ranks transport only. No MPICH C source is linked, compiled, or
vendored; there is no FFI to any system MPI.

