UPSTREAM VERSION — NOT RECORDED BY THE ORIGINAL CRATE, AND NOT DETERMINABLE FROM IT
(gh:#1435, investigated 2026-11-13). The crate (created 2026-07-23, commit 74377bf28)
names two MPICH routines in its doc comments, `MPIR_Bcast_intra_binomial` and
`MPIR_Reduce_intra_binomial`, and `MPIR_Comm_split_impl` for `split`. Evidence:
  * The routine file names `src/mpi/coll/bcast/bcast_intra_binomial.c` and
    `src/mpi/coll/reduce/reduce_intra_binomial.c` exist in every tag from `v3.3` to
    `v4.3.2` and not in `v3.2.1` (listed with `git ls-tree` on a clone). So the port was
    written against **MPICH 3.3 or later**.
  * The binomial algorithm itself is unchanged between `v3.3.2` and `v4.3.2`
    (`diff -w` of `reduce_intra_binomial.c`: only `errflag` plumbing, `MPI_Aint` counts
    and `MPIR_THREADCOMM_RANK_SIZE`). The crate's loops match it exactly in every tag, so
    no version is excluded within that range.
  * Nothing else in the crate (code, comments, tests, `Cargo.toml`, the commit message,
    the issue text it came from) names a version, a commit or a source file, so the
    version **cannot be determined; the best-supported statement is "MPICH >= 3.3, most
    likely the current 4.x line"** (4.x is a guess from the date: the crate was written
    in July 2026, when 4.3.x was current; this is not evidence about what was read).
  * Differential results are therefore reported against **MPICH 4.2.0** (Ubuntu 24.04
    package `mpich 4.2.0-5build3`, built `ch4:ucx`), chosen because it is the version
    installable here, not because the port was translated from it. The algorithms the
    port follows (`reduce_intra_binomial`, `bcast_intra_binomial`,
    `allreduce_intra_recursive_doubling`, `reduce_intra_reduce_scatter_gather`) are
    unchanged in structure between v3.3 and v4.3.2, so a different 4.x version is not
    expected to move the result; that was not run (`Not re-checked`).
  * Routines translated on 2026-11-13 (gh:#1435), with the tag they were read from:
    `MPIR_Allreduce_intra_recursive_doubling` (v4.2.0, same algorithm in v3.3..v4.3.2)
    and `MPIR_Reduce_intra_reduce_scatter_gather` (v4.2.0).
